Files on this disk include:

fdj.com         Format a 5 or 8 inch floppy disk.
formatmw.com    Format a hard disk with the HDDMA controller.
formatmw.doc    Documentation for the HDCA formatting program.
check.com       Checks the integrity of an HDDMA drive.
ramchk1.com	Check the integrity of main memory.
down.com	M10/M16 winchester head park program.  Run this
		program before you power down or move the system.

djboot.com      Boot Micronix from a 5 or 8 inch floppy.
m5boot.com      Boot Micronix from an M5  drive with the HDDMA controller.
m10boot.com     Boot Micronix from an M10 drive with the HDDMA controller.
m16boot.com     Boot Micronix from an M16 drive with the HDDMA controller.

djload          These are versions of the above bootstrap programs
m5load		 suitable for loading onto the system tracks of a 5 inch
m10load          floppy disk. For example, if you do a "sysgen m10load" to
m16load          a 5 inch floppy, then as long as you have that floppy in
                 drive A, pressing RESET will boot Micronix from the M10.
